PHASE 6 — MCP BANKING TOOLS

The following are already implemented and working:

- Azure SQL database
- EF Core model and migration
- Synthetic banking data
- PIN authentication
- Server-side CustomerSession
- Authenticated CustomerId resolution
- Read-only BankingService
- Protected banking REST APIs
- Ownership enforcement

Do NOT redo any of these.

Implement the MCP layer for the Nova AI Banking Assistant.

==================================================
ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

The existing project:

src/NovaBanking.McpServer

must expose the banking operations as MCP tools.

The MCP layer must NOT directly query the database.

MCP tools must call the existing protected application/service layer.

The architecture must remain:

MCP Tool
   ↓
IBankingService
   ↓
ownership enforcement
   ↓
authenticated CustomerId
   ↓
EF Core
   ↓
Azure SQL

The LLM must never receive unrestricted database access.

==================================================
TOOLS
==================================================

Implement these MCP tools:

1. GetCustomerProfile()

2. GetAccountSummary()

3. GetAccountBalance(accountId)

4. GetRecentTransactions(accountId, count)

5. GetLoanSummary(loanId)

6. GetCreditCardSummary(cardId)

Each tool must return structured, safe data.

Do NOT expose:
- PINs
- PIN hashes
- session tokens
- passwords
- SQL connection strings
- full card numbers
- unnecessary sensitive identifiers

==================================================
AUTHENTICATION / CUSTOMER OWNERSHIP
==================================================

CRITICAL:

MCP must NOT accept an arbitrary CustomerId parameter for customer-specific operations.

Do NOT implement:

GetAccountSummary(customerId)

GetCustomerProfile(customerId)

or any equivalent pattern where the LLM chooses CustomerId.

The authenticated server-side session remains the authority.

The MCP layer must use the existing authenticated customer context/application service.

If the current MCP server runs as a separate process and therefore cannot directly access the ASP.NET Core request/session context, do NOT invent a security bypass.

Instead, inspect the current architecture and implement the safest integration pattern that preserves the rule:

CustomerId comes from authenticated server-side context, NOT from LLM input.

If a transport/context bridge is required, document it clearly and keep it server-controlled.

==================================================
TOOL PARAMETERS
==================================================

GetCustomerProfile:
- no parameters

GetAccountSummary:
- no parameters

GetAccountBalance:
- accountId only

GetRecentTransactions:
- accountId
- count

GetLoanSummary:
- loanId only

GetCreditCardSummary:
- cardId only

The identifiers are resource selectors, NOT authorization identities.

The underlying BankingService must continue enforcing:

resource.CustomerId == authenticatedCustomerId

==================================================
MCP TOOL DESCRIPTIONS
==================================================

Give every tool a clear description explaining:
- what it does
- that it is read-only
- what parameters it accepts
- that customer ownership is enforced server-side

Do not allow tools for:
- transfers
- payments
- card blocking
- PIN changes
- credit decisions
- account mutations
- loan mutations
- credit-card mutations

==================================================
MCP SERVER CONFIGURATION
==================================================

Inspect the existing NovaBanking.McpServer project and implement MCP using the appropriate current MCP .NET package/version already selected by the solution.

Do not randomly introduce unrelated MCP frameworks.

Keep the MCP server focused on the case-study tool allowlist.

If the MCP project currently lacks the required packages, add only the necessary packages.

Do not add Azure OpenAI, Semantic Kernel, RAG, or Azure AI Search yet.

==================================================
ERROR HANDLING
==================================================

MCP tools must return safe errors.

Do not expose:
- SQL exceptions
- stack traces
- connection strings
- credentials
- internal authentication details

A resource that does not belong to the authenticated customer must not leak whether that resource exists.

==================================================
TESTING
==================================================

Add focused MCP tests covering:

- GetCustomerProfile works for an authenticated customer
- GetAccountSummary works for an authenticated customer
- GetAccountBalance works for an owned account
- GetRecentTransactions works for an owned account
- GetLoanSummary works for an owned loan
- GetCreditCardSummary works for an owned card
- unauthenticated requests are rejected
- another customer's account cannot be accessed
- another customer's loan cannot be accessed
- another customer's credit card cannot be accessed
- CustomerId cannot be supplied by the LLM to override authentication

Keep tests deterministic.

